{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"85ed775e3afd41705d1c04f93a596f343be1fdee20142f577985b447846a1727","packTokens":2462,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":208,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":790,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1358,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees can sign in using authorized Folio3 Google accounts and have employee and vehicle profiles populated or registered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can release today's parking and schedule releases up to 30 days ahead.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees without dedicated parking can receive notifications and claim available spaces first-come, first-served.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Use license plate recognition to verify temporary parking authorizations at the entrance and record verification attempts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Track parking utilization and automatically email weekly reports to designated stakeholders.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Who receives a push notification when a space becomes available, and what should happen if delivery fails or a recipient has notifications disabled?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Notify all eligible employees without dedicated parking; availability remains claimable in the app even if a push notification is not delivered.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What exact actions may Parking Administrators perform, especially when a holder's release has already been claimed and requires administrator intervention?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Manage employee and parking records, configuration, and reports; also reverse a claimed release when needed, recording the intervention.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"What application access, if any, does a Security Guard need for entrance verification and recording entry status?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Provide a guard-facing view of verification results and a way to record whether the vehicle entered.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Can an employee without dedicated parking claim more than one temporary space for the same date, and can they cancel or relinquish a claim before entry?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allow at most one claim per employee per date, with no user cancellation after a successful claim.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How should daily/weekly utilization and the overall utilization percentage be calculated, including the denominator and the treatment of released but unclaimed spaces?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Define utilization as occupied spaces divided by total available spaces for each reporting period; report released and claimed totals separately and exclude released-but-unclaimed spaces from occupied counts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"May employees add, update, or deactivate their registered vehicle details after first-time setup, or must changes be made by an administrator?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Employees can manage their own vehicle records; administrators can also manage them.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"When a claimant has multiple registered vehicles, which plate should be authorized for that temporary parking claim?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Require the employee to select one registered vehicle when claiming; authorize only that plate for the claim.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"How will entry events for stickered dedicated vehicles be captured for utilization, given that those vehicles bypass system verification?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Have the LPR system record their plate-entry events without requiring authorization verification.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Require Google authentication to identify an account authorized for Folio3 before granting an employee session; refresh employee profiles and parking assignments from corporate directory and current parking records, deny dashboard access with retry or support guidance if the profile is unavailable, and populate dedicated employee and vehicle details.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Require non-dedicated employees without a registered vehicle to register at least one license plate before vehicle-dependent actions; show first-time employees the registration screen and returning employees a dashboard prompt while blocking those actions until a plate is registered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Allow employees to add, update, or deactivate only their own vehicle records, and allow Parking Administrators to manage employee vehicle records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Provide the employee mobile application on iOS and Android, and make its main flows and the guard-facing view conform to WCAG 2.1 AA.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Treat dedicated spaces as reserved for their assigned holders on operating days unless released; let holders release today's space with one action, see its current status, schedule operating-day releases within the next 30 calendar dates, and cancel an unclaimed release.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Make releases claimable at the configured daily release time when released earlier, or immediately when released at or after that time; allow Parking Administrators to reverse claimed releases and record the intervention.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Notify every eligible non-dedicated employee with push notifications enabled when spaces become available, while keeping spaces claimable in the application if notification delivery fails or notifications are disabled.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Allocate each released space to the first successfully committed eligible claim, reject competing claims and duplicate same-day claims by an employee, and return and display the current available-space count.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Require a claimant to select one registered vehicle and authorize only that vehicle's plate; prevent employees from cancelling or relinquishing successful temporary claims.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Assign temporary claims to a configured floor with the fewest current temporary allocations and return and display that floor.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Allow Parking Administrators to manage employee and parking records, operating-day calendars, release-time settings, floor capacities, report settings, and stakeholder email addresses; restrict these and report-management actions to authenticated Parking Administrators.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Ignore pedestrians, motorcycles, and other non-car objects for vehicle authorization; record plate-entry events for vehicles with permanent Folio3 parking stickers without temporary-authorization verification.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"For non-stickered vehicles, normalize plate case and permitted spacing, require an exact match to a current-day temporary authorization, and activate the green indicator only for a match.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Fail closed when a plate is unreadable or the camera, indicator, connection, or authorization service is unavailable; keep the green indicator inactive, alert security for service failures, and record failures when service is restored.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Record each entrance verification attempt with its timestamp, plate when available, verification result, and entry status; provide Security Guards a view of these results and a way to record whether each vehicle entered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"At reporting-period close, record unused dedicated parking when the holder did not release or use the space, and unused temporary parking when the claimant's registered vehicle did not enter.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Calculate utilization as occupied spaces divided by total available spaces, report released and claimed totals separately, and exclude released-but-unclaimed spaces from occupied counts; provide daily and weekly values and the total available-space denominator.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Generate and email the weekly utilization report to configured stakeholder addresses at the configured Monday report time in the office's local timezone, including unused-parking records, daily and weekly utilization, released totals, temporary-claim totals, and utilization percentage.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Provide Parking Administrators with on-screen parking reports, filters, and CSV export, and do not apply automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties based on utilization records.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}